{"context": "A research team is designing an LLM monitor that reviews agent trajectories and flags covertly misaligned behavior. The monitor consists of an LLM plus a prompt, and it must output something that can be turned into a detection decision and evaluated against ground-truth labels. The team needs to settle the format of the monitor's output before running experiments.\n\nQuestion: What output format should the monitor use to express its suspicion of a trajectory?", "options": ["Require the monitor to output an integer suspicion score on a one-to-ten scale rather than a binary flag for each reviewed trajectory.", "Require a structured output with a suspicion score and a short rationale per trajectory, so detection reduces to thresholding the score against labels."], "principles": [], "persona": "", "past_choices": []}
